-- title:
--   Uniformiser generates a prime ideal of the j-chart algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number, $L$ a field of characteristic zero, and $A$ a discrete valuation domain with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, such that the image of $M'$ in the residue field of $A$ is nonzero; let $\varpi \in A$ be a generator of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField M' ⊤)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH M' ⊤)` attached to level $M'$ with full group $H = \top \le (\mathbb{Z}/M')^{\times}$; $K$ carries an $A$-algebra structure compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be an element, assumed nonzero, whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157)$\,= q^{-1}\cdot\,$(the rational $j$-numerator power series). Then, in the subalgebra $B =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` of $K$ consisting of all elements of $K$ integral over $A[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin A {j}`, the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ is prime.
--
--   This is good reduction of $X_0(M')$ at a place of residue characteristic not dividing $M'$, expressed in the two-chart normalisation model: the special fibre at $\varpi$ of the normalisation of the $j$-line inside the level-$M'$ $q$-expansion field is integral. It is used in the analysis of the $j$-finite chart algebra at level $\Gamma_0(M')$, in particular for Dedekind-domain and residue-field statements about that special fibre and for unramifiedness of chart polynomials at height-one primes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isPrime_span_algebraMap_chartAlgFin_xHFunctionField_top_of_natCast_ne_zero.lean

